 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It' often split fifty fifty between the couple and each parents' family. Some couples also add small gift to each parent. That's the old way. These days, couples often just set budget together and don' worry too much about who pays for what. Not rude at all, it's practical. Your parents are welcome to chip in however they like, and your fiancé's family can do the same. Then it' your wedding, your budget, and your day. You could ask them gently to add to the fun fund for the honeymoon instead. That's the best approach. They' probably appreciate it.",
